OL,3,AUS Army says controlled blast of
OL,4,Aexplosives in Iowa was 'huge success'
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe US Army says a controlled blast of
OL,7,Fdegraded explosives in Middletown, Iowa
OL,8,Fwas a "huge success"
OL,10,FSmoke could be seen rising into the sky
OL,11,Fshortly after 09:00 local time - in a
OL,12,Fnews conference afterwards, Maj Gen
OL,13,FEric Shirley says the army reduced the
OL,14,Frisk "as close to zero as is absolute
OL,15,Fhumanly possible"
OL,17,FThe controlled detonation of lead azide
OL,18,F- a highly volatile compound - was
OL,19,Fnecessary to prevent an unplanned
OL,20,Fexplosion, the army says
OL,23,APub: 25-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,317,300,200,140,0,100
